      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Antigravity pace",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Add Antigravity usage pace support for session and weekly quota windows.\r\n- Render pace details for Antigravity quota-summary rows in the menu card.\r\n- Fall back to legacy Antigravity family quota lanes for the menu bar icon when quota-summary data is unavailable.\r\n- Add focused tests covering Antigravity pace text, quota-summary rows, legacy model quota rows, and icon fallback behavior.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\n\r\nAntigravity quota-summary data can provide fixed session and weekly lanes, but older/local legacy snapshots may only populate representative `primary` and `secondary` model quota windows. Without fallback handling, the menu bar icon can appear empty even though usable quota data exists.\r\n\r\nLegacy Antigravity rows also need pace context, but mutating their raw `windowMinutes` would blur the distinction between legacy model quotas and explicit quota-summary windows. This keeps the source data intact while rendering expected 5-hour session pacing where appropriate.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- `swift test --filter antigravity`\r\n- `make check`\r\n- `make test`\r\n\r\n## Screenshot\r\n\r\nbefore\r\n<img width=\"311\" height=\"255\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-05 at 16 03 32\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce5829a0-9720-4484-bd9c-910e6f4f33ab\" />\r\n\r\nafter\r\n<img width=\"309\" height=\"285\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-05 at 4 03 46 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7aca50f-163f-45cf-a4fa-8a642478e49a\" />\r\n",
        "branch": "codex/add-antigravity-pace",
